From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] CHROMIUM: LSM: build report() for the overlayfs check too

The overlayfs check in chromiumos_security_sb_mount() calls report()
unconditionally, but report() is only compiled when
NO_UNPRIVILEGED_UNSAFE_MOUNTS or NO_SYMLINK_MOUNT is enabled. NickelOS
turns both off (Flatpak's bubblewrap mounts inside user namespaces and
through symlinked paths), so build report() unconditionally.

---
--- a/security/chromiumos/lsm.c
+++ b/security/chromiumos/lsm.c
@@ -51,8 +51,6 @@
 }
 __setup("chromiumos.allow_overlayfs", allow_overlayfs_set);
 
-#if defined(CONFIG_SECURITY_CHROMIUMOS_NO_UNPRIVILEGED_UNSAFE_MOUNTS) || \
-	defined(CONFIG_SECURITY_CHROMIUMOS_NO_SYMLINK_MOUNT)
 static void report(const char *origin, const struct path *path, char *operation)
 {
 	char *alloced = NULL, *cmdline;
@@ -85,7 +83,6 @@
 	kfree(cmdline);
 	kfree(alloced);
 }
-#endif
 
 static int chromiumos_security_sb_mount(const char *dev_name,
 					const struct path *path,
